menu "Device spoofing"

config DEVSPOOF
	bool "Per-app device identity spoofing"
	depends on KSU
	default y
	help
	  Allow Kernel Control to report a different CPU, GPU, SoC and memory
	  size to selected apps.  Settings are written to
	  /sys/kernel/device_spoof by the module.

	  This does not hide the real values from root or from the kernel
	  itself; it only changes the procfs and sysfs files that apps read.

endmenu
